      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-108861",
      ":question/problem": "Let $X_{1}\u223cPo(4)$ and $X_{2}\u223cPo(10)$ be independent, and $Y = X_{1} + X_{2}$. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $M_{Y}(t) = M_{X_{1}}(t) + M_{X_{2}}(t)$\n2. $Y=^(d)X_{1}X_{2}$\n3. $Y\u223cPo(14)$\n\n*Hint: The moment-generating function of a Poisson random variable $X\u223cPo(\u03bb)$ is given by*\n$M_{X}(t) = e^{\u03bb(e^{t} - 1)}, t \u2208 R$."
