      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-108873",
      ":question/problem": "Let $X_{1}\u223cB(4, 0.1)$ and $X_{2}\u223cB(4, 0.3)$ be independent, and $Y = X_{1} + X_{2}$. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $M_{Y}(t) = M_{X_{1}}(t) \\cdot M_{X_{2}}(t)$\n2. $Y=^(d)X_{1} \\cdot X_{2}$\n3. $Y\u223cB(4, 0.4)$\n\n*Hint: The moment-generating function of a binomial random variable $X\u223cB(n, p)$ is given by*\n$M_{X}(t) = (1 - p + pe^{t})^{n}, t \u2208 R$."
